WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
A battery pack holds
three cells end to end,

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.560
each one 1.5 volts.

3
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:10.890
All facing the same way, their
emfs add: 4.5 volts in total.

4
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.710
Now slip the middle cell
in the wrong way round.

5
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.350
Nothing else changes.

6
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.990
What does the pack give now?

7
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:17.910
The same?

8
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:18.720
Less?

9
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.000
Nothing at all?

10
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.460
In this mission, you'll
go once round a loop,

11
00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:26.720
cell by cell, keeping track
of which way each cell faces.

12
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:31.000
Then you'll find the current in one
branch of a mixed resistor circuit.

13
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:35.630
Your mission: predict the total voltage
of the pack with one cell reversed.
